Add a notification bell for GDMS failures + a backfill date picker (v0.125)

Dan tested v0.124's recall/log feature and it worked as expected, then
raised a real problem: sometimes new stock gets despatched before
Grandstream has finished assigning it to our channel on their side, so
our /assign call fails for it - and until now that failure was only
visible if someone thought to go check the GDMS log. His two ideas:

1. A notification bell (top-right, number bubble) that surfaces "GDMS
   Error" and takes you straight to the filtered log when clicked.
2. A date picker next to "Run GDMS end-of-day now" so a bad day (GDMS
   down, or a batch that failed for the reason above) can be backfilled
   once it clears, rather than only ever re-running today's despatches.

He also asked me to confirm an assumption: that retrying via the
per-order button would pick up a previously-failed device. Confirmed,
no code change needed - StockItem.gdmsSyncedAt is only ever set on
success, so a failed device is naturally picked up fresh by the next
run of any kind.

Implemented:

- New general-purpose `notifications` table (migration V53) -
  deliberately not GDMS-specific, so it can back other notification
  types later (Dan's mentioned wanting a reminder system at some
  point) without rework. `NotificationService`/`NotificationController`:
  GET /notifications (recent 30), GET /notifications/unread-count
  (polled every 30s for the badge), POST /notifications/mark-all-read.

- `GdmsChannelService` now raises one GDMS_FAILURE notification per
  assign/recall call that has any failed MAC - once per call, not once
  per internal 100-MAC batch, so a whole failed run doesn't spam the
  bell. The notification links to /gdms-log?from=<today>&to=<today>&
  status=FAILURE. Confirmed via two design questions with Dan: the
  notifications table is general-purpose (not GDMS-only), and the
  badge clears the instant the bell is opened rather than only once a
  specific failure has actually been viewed.

- New floating NotificationBell component (fixed top-right - this
  app's Layout has no header bar to live in, sidebar-only) - badge,
  dropdown of recent notifications, click-to-navigate, click-outside
  to close.

- GdmsLog.tsx now reads its initial from/to/status filters from the
  URL query string on mount, so a notification's link lands already
  filtered to the right day and FAILURE status.

- SettingsController's run-end-of-day endpoint now takes an optional
  `date` param (defaults to today); Settings.tsx grew a date input
  next to the button. Sync log source reads "Manual" for today,
  "Manual (backfill <date>)" for a picked-back date, so it's obvious
  on the log which runs were a live catch-up versus a backfill.

